  "details": "In Unity Editor, modified Parameter Drivers Behaviors are not saved to disk if it's the last modification of the animator.\nIf such a modification is made, an avatar can be uploaded with a modified VRC Avatar Parameter Driver that contains the new values, but as soon as Unity Editor is closed then opened again, then uploading the same avatar will result in a VRC Avatar Parameter Driver that contains the previous values.\nUse case:\nI tried to tweak driver values between multiple avatar uploads in order to encode parameter presets, and then uploading the avatar. However, reuploading the avatar again the next day with tweaked materials without touching the animator resulted in different driver parameters values being applied.\nHow to reproduce:\n- Using VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2021.02.23.11.41_Public.unitypackage\n- Open Unity\n- Create a new animator controller\n- Open the Animator editor\n- In the Parameters tab, Create a new float parameter\n- Add a State in the base layer\n- Add a VRC Avatar Parameter Driver behavior to that state\n- Add a Parameter to that VRC Avatar Parameter Driver\n- Set the value to 0.5\n- Close Unity Editor\n- Start Unity Editor\n- Open the Animator editor\n- Click the state\n- Set the value to 0.7\n- Do not change anything else in the animator, including moving a state around or hitting CTRL-S\n- * See additional footnotes\n- Close Unity Editor\n- Start Unity Editor\n- Open the Animator editor\n- Click the state\nObserved:\n- The value is 0.5\nExpected:\n- The value is 0.7\n* Footnotes: Other operations can be done here, including uploading the avatar with that animator controller. When uploading the avatar, the parameter will have the expected value of 0.7, but when Unity Editor is closed and opened again, then the value of the animator will be 0.5",
